  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Kuldeep vs State Of U.P. on 22 October, 2019 Author: Siddharth Bench: Siddharth",
    "facts": "Offence under sections 60 of Excise Act is bailable and trible by Magistrate. False recovery has been alleged. The applicant is languishing in jail since 29.08.2019, who is not a previous convict.",
    "arguments": "On the other hand learned AGA has opposed the prayer for bail. Keeping in view the nature of the offence, evidence on record regarding complicity of the accused, submissions of the learned counsel for the parties noted herein above, larger mandate of the Article 21 of the Constitution of India and the dictum of Apex Court in the case of Dataram Singh Vs. State of U.P. and another reported in (2018)3 SCC 22 and without expressing any opinion on the merits of Kuldeep vs State Of U.P. on 22 October, 2019 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/12507284/ 1 the case, the Court is of the view that the applicant has made out a case for bail.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
